  "description": "ONAVIK crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C73 H82 Dy4 N4 O19,C6 H16 N1 1+,2(C4 H10 O1),N1 O3 1-. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.491-3.847 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.86-109.98°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C73H82Dy4N4O19·C6H16N·NO3·2(C4H10O) (table C87H118N6O24Dy4). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
